    {
      "name": "places/ChIJK3xb0mDzaS4RyQOmsFcW-_M/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURJdS1fMG5BRRAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "7 years ago",
      "rating": 3,
      "text": {
        "text": "Super duper sweett!\nRecommended ONLY IF YOU ARE A SWEET TOOTH!\n\nWe came for the kunafe, it's a sweet pastry made of cheese, but since we came from far away might as well try the baklava. Well I don't paeticularly fond of sweets, so it's hell for me.\n\nTLDR; DON'T come if you don't like sweet. It's expensive and not worth the price IMO. Come for the experience ONLY if you love sweet. I've warned you.\n\nBaklava - pastry from sugary water.\nThat explains it enough, the sugary layer is so thick you can actually see it, I can only taste sugar on each bite abd the chocolate is soooo chocolatey, if you LOVE sweet by all means try it you might even like it.\n\nKunafe, it's cheese, but I can still taste the sweet in it. It's okay but I won't come to eat it again.\n\nTurkish tea, the bitter taste is just right with the super sweet baklava and kunafe, but a bit taste like SariWangi at first. Very small for a tea at that price, starbucks doesn't sound so expensive anymore.\n\nThe café is small but comfy, the employee are nice and kind, clean kitchen, everything else is good.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "originalText": {
        "text": "Super duper sweett!\nRecommended ONLY IF YOU ARE A SWEET TOOTH!\n\nWe came for the kunafe, it's a sweet pastry made of cheese, but since we came from far away might as well try the baklava. Well I don't paeticularly fond of sweets, so it's hell for me.\n\nTLDR; DON'T come if you don't like sweet. It's expensive and not worth the price IMO. Come for the experience ONLY if you love sweet. I've warned you.\n\nBaklava - pastry from sugary water.\nThat explains it enough, the sugary layer is so thick you can actually see it, I can only taste sugar on each bite abd the chocolate is soooo chocolatey, if you LOVE sweet by all means try it you might even like it.\n\nKunafe, it's cheese, but I can still taste the sweet in it. It's okay but I won't come to eat it again.\n\nTurkish tea, the bitter taste is just right with the super sweet baklava and kunafe, but a bit taste like SariWangi at first. Very small for a tea at that price, starbucks doesn't sound so expensive anymore.\n\nThe café is small but comfy, the employee are nice and kind, clean kitchen, everything else is good.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
